comments.body:
@MasterPlexus Having both Apps on "Power whitelist" is prerequisite... But even with that it still happens, that sometimes ruffy gets stuck (non-responsive) or terminates (doesn't happen so much). 

So AAPS and Combo worked perfectly for me when I had Android 8.1 (OnePlus 5T), then I upgraded to 9, and now here and there happens that AAPS stops communicating (this happens for me maybe once every 2 weeks, so NOT often), in meantime my OnePlus was upgraded to 10, and it happens less often (but it still happens). When I used Combo on Samsung S9 with Android 8.1, this happened much more often (1x week), before that I used Combo on Samsung A6, and there it happened every few days (that phone was Android 7 that was rooted).

@leonbohmann 
Is this problem for you that you need to restart AAPS? How often does it happen? I mean there is alarm that you can set that would notify you if pump hasn't communicated for last 30 minutes.

From my times with my first phone, I always modify my Combo driver a little, so that it shows how many communication errors it had (its just counter that gets reset, when we get successful communication). I was thinking of adding that into main code, but haven't gotten around to it yet...
